# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically asked to review what.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO DEFAULT OWNER LINE. A `*` rule would route every
# pull request at the same group, which is the bottleneck this file exists to
# remove.
#
# OWNERS ARE A TEAM, NOT A PERSON (2026-08-31, on the move to the `samomdkku`
# organisation). A named individual here does not switch off when that person
# graduates — it keeps blocking every change, waiting for an approval that is
# not coming. Membership of @samomdkku/maintainers is the thing to edit, and
# any org owner can edit it.
#
# ⚠️ The team must stay VISIBLE (privacy `closed`, not `secret`) and hold WRITE
# on this repo. GitHub silently ignores a code-owner team missing either, which
# looks exactly like the rule working. Anything not listed here still needs one approving review
# (branch protection), but from ANY collaborator.
#
# Listed here = the load-bearing surfaces, taken from the "touch zones" table in
# CONTRIBUTING.md. Every one of them has cost this repo a real outage or a real
# bug; the write-ups are in docs/mistakes/.
#
# NOTE: this file makes GitHub REQUEST a review. It only BLOCKS a merge once
# `require_code_owner_reviews` is enabled on the branch protection rule — see
# docs/TEAM-WORKFLOW.md §8a.

# Auth, the Supabase client, and anything that talks to the database
/src/js/auth.js        @samomdkku/maintainers
/src/js/db.js          @samomdkku/maintainers

# Notifications and uploads — wrong here is a silent production outage
/src/js/notify.js      @samomdkku/maintainers
/src/js/uploads.js     @samomdkku/maintainers

# Schema is the source of truth for the live database
/supabase/             @samomdkku/maintainers

# Deploy plumbing, the notify service, nginx
/server/               @samomdkku/maintainers

# Apps Script — Discord webhooks live here; a redeploy hits production at once
/appscript/            @samomdkku/maintainers

# Proof scripts and migration tooling
/tools/                @samomdkku/maintainers

# CI, and this file
/.github/              @samomdkku/maintainers

# Agent context: charged to every session on the team, byte-capped
/CLAUDE.md             @samomdkku/maintainers
/.claude/              @samomdkku/maintainers

# The handoff
/STATE.md              @samomdkku/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ฝ่าย CONTRIBUTIONS — added 2026-08-27. See docs/DEPT-TOOLS.md §0b.
#
# There is ONE workflow: a ฝ่าย member uses the identical pull-request pipeline
# as the dev team. The whole difference between them lives in THIS FILE, which
# is how large orgs do it — same process, different paths you may merge into.
#
# These paths do not all exist yet. A rule for a path that does not exist is
# harmless and is here so the ownership question is settled BEFORE the first
# contribution arrives, not during it.

# The line that decides what is reachable and who may see it.
/src/data/tools.js     @samomdkku/maintainers

# A tool that runs INSIDE the app bundle — it can reach what the app can reach.
/src/tools/            @samomdkku/maintainers

# The data doors. Each one answers a single question and carries the access
# rule. This is the "who may see what" decision, which is the one thing a
# contributor may never write.
/src/js/data/          @samomdkku/maintainers

# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED: /public/embed/**
#
# A contributed page in the sandbox frame reaches NOTHING — no app DOM, no
# session, no database. Any collaborator may approve it, and that is the point:
# a rule here would route every poster and infographic back to one person and
# rebuild the bottleneck this file exists to remove.
